# =====================================================================
# AROIDPEDIA - .gitignore
#
# This repo is BOTH the CDN for the live site (everything under docs/ is
# served from GitHub Pages) and the host for the refresh automations. So
# the rule here is narrow on purpose: ignore only build litter, and never
# use a broad glob that could swallow a published asset.
#
# ⚠ In particular there is NO "*cache*" rule. docs/search-index-cache.json
# is a PUBLISHED, COMMITTED file - the per-page lastmod record that makes
# the nightly search-index crawl incremental. Ignoring it would throw the
# cache away with each runner and quietly send every run back to crawling
# all 380+ pages from cold, with nothing appearing to be wrong. The build
# caches below are therefore named exactly, never matched by pattern.
# =====================================================================

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ---- Node -------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in this repo needs node_modules, but the climate builder does
# `npm i geotiff` in its own workspace, and a stray install here would be
# a very large accident.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ---- Builder download caches ------------------------------------------
# Natural Earth, WorldClim and POWO responses. These live on the Drive
# beside their builders and are tens to hundreds of MB; the pipeline
# READMEs say "never commit it" for each one. Listed here as a backstop in
# case a builder is ever run from inside the repo.
ne-cache/
ne-cache-hd/
climate-cache/
powo-cache/

# ---- Local backup copies ----------------------------------------------
# House convention on the Drive is to park a pre-change copy beside the
# file: places.json.bak-preIndia, shapes.json.before-laos,
# araceae-tree.v1.json.bak-pre-1.32.0. Those belong in the working folder,
# not in the published artifact - git history is the backup here.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.before-*

# ---- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in this repo reads a .env today. The rule exists so that adding
# one later cannot be committed by reflex.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- OS and editor litter ---------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---- Explicit keeps ---------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces: these are published assets and must always be tracked,
# whatever a future rule above might otherwise match.
!docs/search-index-cache.json
!docs/**
